#!/usr/bin/env python3
r"""
tools/pipe/pr-merge — sanctioned merge protocol wrapper + pr_merged v3 span.

Usage:
  python tools/pipe/pr-merge <pr-number>
  python tools/pipe/pr-merge --confirm <pr-number>

Real-path repoint target for reviewer.md's APPROVE-merge action + BEHIND-
retry loop (slice #1078 / PRD #1075 criterion 1): embodies the existing
retry protocol (gh pr update-branch -> poll ci checks -> retry --auto,
bounded 3 attempts total) so the reviewer's inline prose collapses to one
wrapper call. NEVER plain `--squash` — always `--squash --auto` (no
`--delete-branch`: worktree-guard prune owns branch cleanup post-merge;
the flag only produced post-merge noise — "failed to delete local
branch ... used by worktree" — that masked genuine merge success; slice
#1100).

FALSE-NEGATIVE FIX (slice #1100, root-cause proven live on PR #1095's
merge): `gh pr merge` can exit non-zero AFTER the merge already
succeeded server-side (the "Auto merge is not allowed for this
repository" quirk observed here). `_do_default` therefore REST-checks
merged state (via `_check_merged_once`) before concluding failure on
ANY non-zero gh exit — never trusting a raw exit code alone to mean
"no merge happened".

BOUNDED-BUDGET DESIGN (reviewer round-1 finding #2, PR #1089): a single
invocation of this script — whether the default mode or --confirm mode —
NEVER blocks past PR_MERGE_BUDGET_S (default ~90s), so it always finishes
well inside the calling agent's tool-invocation timeout (Bash tool default
120s / max 600s). Long CI waits are handled by RE-INVOKING the script, not
by one process blocking for minutes:

  - Default invocation: attempts the merge (with the existing bounded
    BEHIND-retry sub-loop) and then polls the REST API for a confirmed
    MERGED state, but only for up to the remaining budget. If confirmed
    within budget -> appends the pr_merged span, exits 0. If the merge
    command itself never succeeds within budget -> exits 1 (no span, no
    "pending" — the side effect did not happen). If the merge command DID
    succeed/queue but MERGED isn't confirmed within budget -> prints a
    loud `MERGE-PENDING: run tools/pipe/pr-merge --confirm <n> to finish`
    line and exits 3 (never 0, never a span — the caller must re-invoke).
  - `--confirm <n>`: idempotent re-entry. First checks the trace log for
    an existing pr_merged span for this PR (IDEMPOTENCE GUARD — never
    double-append); if found, prints "already recorded" and exits 0
    without any gh calls. Otherwise polls REST for up to the budget; on
    confirmed MERGED, re-checks the idempotence guard (race-safety) then
    appends the span and exits 0. If still pending, repeats the same
    MERGE-PENDING / exit-3 contract as the default invocation.

On a confirmed MERGED state (checked via the REST API — `gh api
repos/<owner>/<repo>/pulls/<n>` — not GraphQL, per the "if gh GraphQL flakes
use REST" guidance), appends one pr_merged span (attrs: pr, sha) with the
elapsed duration of THIS invocation. Never a silent half-success: either a
span is appended, or the process exits non-zero and writes nothing.

VERDICT ASSERTION (slice #1130 / PRD #1127 criterion 3a, ADR-0076 D3): before
any merge attempt (default mode) or any confirm-poll (--confirm mode, unless
already idempotently recorded), this wrapper refuses to proceed unless the PR
carries a reviewer comment matching the exact `VERDICT:\s*APPROVE` signal
`.claude/hooks/stop-reviewer-gate.sh` already greps (via `gh pr view <n>
--json comments`). Refusal is non-zero exit with a named reason on stderr,
BEFORE any gh side effect. On a confirmed merge, a `verdict` span (attrs:
critic, round, verdict, pr — parsed from that same APPROVE comment) is
appended in addition to the existing pr_merged span (criterion 3b).

RECORD-GREEN CHAINING (slice #1134 / PRD #1127 criterion 4, ADR-0076 D1):
on a FRESHLY confirmed merge (both the default path and `--confirm`
re-entry — never on the already-recorded idempotence shortcut, which does
zero work by design), this wrapper tail-invokes `tools/pipe/record-green`
as a subprocess bounded by pr-merge's own REMAINING wall-clock budget for
THIS invocation — never a fresh budget. The outcome (green recorded /
evaluation failed / budget exhausted before or during the chained call) is
always named on stdout/stderr, never silent. This chained call NEVER flips
pr-merge's own exit code: the merge already succeeded and was already
recorded before the chain runs (mirrors the #1102 non-fatal-enrichment
posture for `tools/promote.sh`'s own span emit).

LANE MODE (slice #1506 / PRD #1501, ADR-0090 D3/D4): when the PR carries the
`lane` label, three additional legs gate on the SAME `gh pr view` call
`_fetch_pr_view` already widened to include `labels,body,headRefName` — no
extra gh call on an ordinary PR:
  - MODEL: refusal (criterion 24) — the APPROVE comment's `MODEL:` line must
    be present, and its whole value must name a Claude Opus model
    (allow-list: `opus`, optional `claude` prefix, optional version); an
    empty value, a placeholder, trailing words, Sonnet, Haiku or any other
    name refuses.
  - Window refusal (criterion 25) — every non-merge commit on the lane's
    head branch must fall inside a recorded `dispatch`->`dispatch_end`
    window on trace_id `lane-<headRefName>`.
  - Close-on-merge (criteria 26 and 27): on confirmed merge, every issue
    named on a whole `Closes #<n>` line of the PR body is closed (a
    `closes #<n>` inside prose closes nothing), and each issue it closed
    gets a comment giving the PR number and the merge sha; an issue whose
    close fails gets no comment and is named on stderr. This runs after
    merge confirmation and before the span append, never on the
    already-recorded idempotence shortcut.

Env overrides (test seam; production defaults are sane real-world values):
  PR_MERGE_BUDGET_S        (default 90) — overall wall-clock budget for ONE
                            invocation (merge attempts + BEHIND checks-poll
                            + REST confirm-poll + the chained record-green
                            call all share this budget)
  PR_MERGE_POLL_INTERVAL_S (default 5)  — sleep between poll iterations
"""
import importlib.util
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from datetime import datetime, timezone

_THIS_DIR = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
_TOOLS_DIR = os.path.dirname(_THIS_DIR)
_TRACE_PY = os.path.join(_TOOLS_DIR, "trace.py")
_RECORD_GREEN = os.path.join(_THIS_DIR, "record-green")

MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3
BUDGET_S = float(os.environ.get("PR_MERGE_BUDGET_S", "90"))
POLL_INTERVAL_S = float(os.environ.get("PR_MERGE_POLL_INTERVAL_S", "5"))


def _load_trace():
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("trace_v3", _TRACE_PY)
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    spec.loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


def _load_pipeline_config():
    # No literal branch names (C1) — the integration branch is resolved
    # only through this module (ADR-0089 D1), same pattern as dispatch's
    # own _load_pipeline_config().
    pc_py = os.path.join(_TOOLS_DIR, "pipeline_config.py")
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("pipeline_config_prmerge", pc_py)
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    spec.loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


def _gh():
    return shutil.which("gh") or "gh"


def _run_gh(args):
    return subprocess.run(
        [_gh()] + args, capture_output=True, text=True, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace",
    )


def _write_stdout_utf8(text):
    """Write `text` to stdout as UTF-8 bytes whatever the console or pipe
    encoding: a cp1252 stdout (Windows) cannot encode e.g. U+2713. A failed
    write raises OSError/ValueError for the caller to handle."""
    sys.stdout.flush()
    buf = getattr(sys.stdout, "buffer", None)
    if buf is None:
        sys.stdout.write(text)
        sys.stdout.flush()
        return
    buf.write(text.encode("utf-8", errors="replace"))
    buf.flush()


def _remote_owner_repo():
    """Resolve owner/repo from `git remote get-url origin` — avoids depending
    on gh's own {owner}/{repo} api templating so this stays stubbable."""
    try:
        url = subprocess.run(
            ["git", "remote", "get-url", "origin"],
            capture_output=True, text=True, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace", check=True,
        ).stdout.strip()
    except Exception:
        return None
    m = re.search(r"[:/]([^/]+)/([^/.]+?)(?:\.git)?$", url)
    if not m:
        return None
    return m.group(1), m.group(2)


def _sleep_until(deadline):
    """Sleep POLL_INTERVAL_S, but never past deadline."""
    remaining = deadline - time.monotonic()
    if remaining > 0:
        time.sleep(min(POLL_INTERVAL_S, remaining))


def _poll_checks_until_green(pr, deadline):
    """Bounded by the shared deadline (NOT an independent long timeout)."""
    while True:
        res = _run_gh(["pr", "checks", str(pr)])
        combined = ((res.stdout or "") + (res.stderr or "")).lower()
        if res.returncode == 0:
            return True
        if "fail" in combined:
            return False
        if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
            return False
        _sleep_until(deadline)


def _check_merged_once(pr):
    """One REST check (not GraphQL). Returns (merged: bool, sha: str|None)."""
    owner_repo = _remote_owner_repo()
    if not owner_repo:
        return False, None
    owner, repo = owner_repo
    res = _run_gh(["api", f"repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{pr}"])
    if res.returncode == 0:
        try:
            data = json.loads(res.stdout)
        except json.JSONDecodeError:
            data = {}
        if data.get("merged"):
            return True, data.get("merge_commit_sha")
    return False, None


def _poll_confirm_merged(pr, deadline):
    """Poll the REST API for merged state, bounded by the shared deadline."""
    while True:
        merged, sha = _check_merged_once(pr)
        if merged:
            return True, sha
        if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
            return False, None
        _sleep_until(deadline)


def _existing_pr_merged_span(trace, pr):
    """IDEMPOTENCE GUARD: scan the trace log for an existing pr_merged span
    for this PR number. Returns the span dict if found, else None."""
    pr_str = str(pr)
    for s in trace.read_spans():
        if s.get("kind") == "pr_merged" and str(s.get("attrs", {}).get("pr")) == pr_str:
            return s
    return None


def _pending_message(pr):
    return f"MERGE-PENDING: run tools/pipe/pr-merge --confirm {pr} to finish"


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RECORD-GREEN CHAINING (slice #1134 / PRD #1127 criterion 4, ADR-0076 D1)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

def _chain_record_green(deadline, sha=None):
    """Tail-invoke tools/pipe/record-green from a FRESHLY confirmed merge,
    bounded by pr-merge's own REMAINING wall-clock budget for THIS
    invocation -- never a fresh budget. Never raises; never changes the
    caller's exit code -- the merge already succeeded and was already
    recorded before this runs, so record-green's outcome (or the budget
    being exhausted before/during the call) is only ever NAMED, honestly,
    on stdout/stderr (mirrors the #1102 non-fatal-enrichment posture).

    `sha` (#1188 / root-cause #1183): the CONFIRMED merge-commit oid this
    invocation already holds from the GitHub REST API, passed straight
    through as record-green's explicit sha argument so the chained call
    certifies the sha that was actually just merged -- never a local
    `origin/<integration>` ref (the configured integration branch,
    ADR-0089 D1) that can be stale by the time this fires (the ci-trust
    fast path, #1163, made the chain fire 2-6s post-merge, which widened
    that exposure). When `sha` is falsy (e.g. the GitHub API response
    omitted merge_commit_sha), falls back to record-green's own no-arg
    fetch-then-resolve path, preserving prior behavior."""
    remaining = deadline - time.monotonic()
    if remaining <= 0:
        print(
            "pr-merge: record-green NOT chained -- pr-merge's budget was "
            "already exhausted confirming the merge; run "
            "'python tools/pipe/record-green' manually to evaluate develop_green",
            file=sys.stderr,
        )
        return
    cmd = [sys.executable, _RECORD_GREEN]
    if sha:
        cmd.append(sha)
    try:
        result = subprocess.run(cmd, timeout=remaining)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        print(
            f"pr-merge: record-green TIMED OUT after {remaining:.0f}s "
            "(pr-merge's remaining budget exhausted) -- develop_green outcome "
            "UNKNOWN; run 'python tools/pipe/record-green' manually",
            file=sys.stderr,
        )
        return
    if result.returncode == 0:
        print("pr-merge: record-green chained -- develop_green recorded")
    else:
        # Names the role, never the resolved branch: this runs after the
        # merge, so a resolver read here could raise (malformed conf) and
        # turn a completed merge into a non-zero exit (ADR-0089 D1).
        print(
            f"pr-merge: record-green chained -- evaluation FAILED "
            f"(exit={result.returncode}); the integration branch is NOT "
            "green (see record-green output above)",
            file=sys.stderr,
        )


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERDICT ASSERTION (slice #1130 / PRD #1127 criterion 3a/3b, ADR-0076 D3)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The exact signal `.claude/hooks/stop-reviewer-gate.sh` greps:
#   gh pr view "$N" --json comments --jq '.comments | map(select(.body |
#     test("VERDICT:\\s*APPROVE"))) | length'
_VERDICT_APPROVE_RE = re.compile(r"VERDICT:\s*APPROVE")
_CRITIC_ATTR_RE = re.compile(r"^CRITIC:\s*(\S+)", re.MULTILINE)
_ROUND_ATTR_RE = re.compile(r"^ROUND:\s*(\S+)", re.MULTILINE)


def _fetch_pr_view(pr):
    """Fetch the PR view via `gh pr view <pr> --json comments,labels,body,
    headRefName` — WIDENED (slice #1506 / ADR-0090 D3/D4) from the original
    `--json comments`-only call stop-reviewer-gate.sh also uses, so the lane
    legs below (label check, close-on-merge, window check) read from this
    SAME gh call rather than issuing a second one. On a non-lane PR the
    extra fields are simply unused -- no new gh call, no behavior change.
    Returns the parsed dict, or None if gh failed or returned unparseable
    output."""
    res = _run_gh(["pr", "view", str(pr), "--json", "comments,labels,body,headRefName"])
    if res.returncode != 0:
        return None
    try:
        return json.loads(res.stdout)
    except json.JSONDecodeError:
        return None


def _find_approve_comment(comments):
    """Return the most recent comment matching the exact `VERDICT:\\s*APPROVE`
    signal stop-reviewer-gate.sh greps, or None if no comment matches."""
    matches = [c for c in comments if _VERDICT_APPROVE_RE.search(c.get("body", "") or "")]
    return matches[-1] if matches else None


def _verdict_attrs(pr, comment):
    """Derive verdict span attrs (critic, round, verdict, pr) from the body
    of the APPROVE comment that satisfied the precondition."""
    body = comment.get("body", "") or ""
    critic_m = _CRITIC_ATTR_RE.search(body)
    round_m = _ROUND_ATTR_RE.search(body)
    return {
        "pr": pr,
        "critic": critic_m.group(1) if critic_m else "unknown",
        "round": round_m.group(1) if round_m else "unknown",
        "verdict": "APPROVE",
    }


def _assert_verdict_or_refuse(pr):
    """Precondition (ADR-0076 D3 / PRD #1127 criterion 3a): refuse (return
    (None, None)) unless the PR carries a reviewer comment matching the exact
    `VERDICT:\\s*APPROVE` signal `.claude/hooks/stop-reviewer-gate.sh` greps.
    A named reason is printed to stderr; the caller exits non-zero having
    performed NO merge attempt and written NO span. On success, returns
    `(comment, view)` — `_verdict_attrs` derives the verdict span from
    `comment`; `view` (labels/body/headRefName) feeds the lane legs below
    (slice #1506) so callers never re-fetch."""
    view = _fetch_pr_view(pr)
    if view is None:
        print(
            f"pr-merge: could not fetch PR #{pr} comments to verify a reviewer "
            "VERDICT: APPROVE -- refusing to merge",
            file=sys.stderr,
        )
        return None, None
    comments = view.get("comments", [])
    comment = _find_approve_comment(comments)
    if comment is None:
        print(
            f"pr-merge: PR #{pr} carries no reviewer comment matching "
            "'VERDICT: APPROVE' -- refusing to merge",
            file=sys.stderr,
        )
        return None, None
    return comment, view


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LANE MODE (slice #1506 / PRD #1501, ADR-0090 D3/D4): MODEL: refusal,
# dispatch-window refusal, close-on-merge -- gated on the "lane" label so
# NONE of these three legs run any extra gh call, print, or refusal on an
# ordinary (non-lane) PR (named risk, PRD #1501 constraint 5).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Criterion 24 / ADR-0090 D4 merge leg 1. The WHOLE line value is read,
# never its first token, and judged against an allow-list rather than a
# denylist: D4 dispatches every lane reviewer with `model: "opus"`, so the
# only accepted value names a Claude Opus model -- `opus`, optionally
# prefixed `claude`, optionally followed by a version (`5-5`, `5.5`,
# `4-1-20250805`), case- and separator-insensitive (`Claude Opus 5.5`).
# Everything else refuses: a missing or empty line, a placeholder (`n/a`,
# `<id>`), trailing words, Sonnet, Haiku, or any other name. `[ \t]*`
# (never `\s*`) keeps an empty `MODEL:` from reading the next line.
_MODEL_LINE_RE = re.compile(r"^MODEL:[ \t]*(.*)$", re.MULTILINE)
_STRONG_MODEL_RE = re.compile(r"^(?:claude-)?opus(?:-\d+(?:[.-]\d+)*)?$")
# Criterion 26: a lane PR closes exactly the issues named on whole
# `Closes #<n>` lines. Prose such as "step 5 (closes #1448)" closes nothing.
# reviewer.md's R-CLOSES lane leg names this same pattern.
_LANE_CLOSES_RE = re.compile(r"^Closes #(\d+)\s*$", re.MULTILINE)


def _is_lane_pr(view):
    """True iff the PR view (from `_fetch_pr_view`) carries the `lane`
    label (ADR-0090 D1 class label; bootstrap.sh's `lane` entry)."""
    if not view:
        return False
    labels = view.get("labels") or []
    names = {l.get("name") for l in labels if isinstance(l, dict)}
    return "lane" in names


def _normalize_model_value(raw):
    """Lower-case, drop surrounding backticks/quotes, and fold runs of
    whitespace or underscores into `-`, so `Claude Opus 5.5` and
    `claude-opus-5.5` compare alike."""
    value = raw.strip().strip("`'\"").strip().lower()
    return re.sub(r"[\s_]+", "-", value)


def _is_strong_model(raw):
    return bool(_STRONG_MODEL_RE.match(_normalize_model_value(raw)))


def _assert_lane_model_or_refuse(pr, approve_comment):
    """Criterion 24: refuse (before any merge call) unless the APPROVE
    comment carries at least one `MODEL:` line and EVERY such line names a
    Claude Opus model (allow-list above). Two lines that disagree are a
    self-contradicting comment, so the leg fails closed."""
    body = approve_comment.get("body", "") or ""
    values = [v.strip() for v in _MODEL_LINE_RE.findall(body)]
    if not values:
        reason = "has no MODEL: line"
    else:
        bad = [v for v in values if not _is_strong_model(v)]
        if not bad:
            return True
        reason = "has MODEL: " + ", ".join(repr(v) for v in bad) + ", which is not a Claude Opus model id"
    print(
        f"pr-merge: lane PR #{pr} refused -- the APPROVE comment {reason} "
        "(ADR-0090 D4: a lane PR merges only on a strong-model review; accepted: "
        "opus, claude-opus-<version>, Claude Opus <version>)",
        file=sys.stderr,
    )
    return False


def _fetch_lane_commits(head_ref):
    """Non-merge commits authored on `head_ref` but not on the configured
    integration branch (C1: resolved via pipeline_config, never a literal),
    as `(sha, authored_ts)` pairs -- `ts` in the same UTC Z-suffixed format
    trace-v3 spans use, so it compares directly against span `ts` strings.
    Returns None if the git plumbing itself fails (treated as refusal by
    the caller -- never a silent pass)."""
    pc = _load_pipeline_config()
    base = pc.integration_branch()
    for ref in (head_ref, base):
        subprocess.run(
            ["git", "fetch", "origin", ref],
            capture_output=True, text=True, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace",
        )
    res = subprocess.run(
        ["git", "log", f"origin/{base}..origin/{head_ref}", "--no-merges", "--pretty=%H %at"],
        capture_output=True, text=True, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace",
    )
    if res.returncode != 0:
        return None
    commits = []
    for line in res.stdout.strip().splitlines():
        if not line.strip():
            continue
        sha, epoch = line.strip().split(" ", 1)
        ts = datetime.fromtimestamp(int(epoch), tz=timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")
        commits.append((sha, ts))
    return commits


def _lane_dispatch_windows(trace, head_ref):
    """The list of `(dispatch_ts, dispatch_end_ts)` windows recorded on
    trace_id `lane-<head_ref>` -- matching pairs by chronological open/close
    order (mirrors dispatch's own last-event-wins span reading, but paired
    rather than reduced to a single active/inactive bit)."""
    spans = trace.read_spans()
    relevant = [
        s for s in spans
        if s.get("trace_id") == f"lane-{head_ref}" and s.get("kind") in ("dispatch", "dispatch_end")
    ]
    relevant.sort(key=lambda s: s.get("ts", ""))
    windows = []
    open_start = None
    for s in relevant:
        if s.get("kind") == "dispatch":
            open_start = s.get("ts")
        elif s.get("kind") == "dispatch_end" and open_start is not None:
            windows.append((open_start, s.get("ts")))
            open_start = None
    return windows


def _assert_lane_window_or_refuse(pr, view):
    """Criterion 25: refuse (before any merge call) when a non-merge commit
    on the lane PR's head branch was authored OUTSIDE every recorded
    `dispatch`->`dispatch_end` window on trace_id `lane-<headRefName>` --
    proof the commit landed via a dispatched implementer turn, not a
    manual out-of-band push."""
    head_ref = view.get("headRefName") or ""
    if not head_ref:
        print(f"pr-merge: lane PR #{pr} refused -- could not resolve headRefName", file=sys.stderr)
        return False
    commits = _fetch_lane_commits(head_ref)
    if commits is None:
        print(f"pr-merge: lane PR #{pr} refused -- could not read its commit history", file=sys.stderr)
        return False
    trace = _load_trace()
    windows = _lane_dispatch_windows(trace, head_ref)
    offenders = [
        sha for sha, ts in commits
        if not any(start <= ts <= end for start, end in windows)
    ]
    if offenders:
        print(
            f"pr-merge: lane PR #{pr} refused -- commit(s) authored outside "
            f"every dispatch window of lane-{head_ref}: {', '.join(offenders)}",
            file=sys.stderr,
        )
        return False
    return True


def _close_lane_issues(view):
    """Criterion 26: close every issue named on a whole `Closes #<n>` line
    of the lane PR's body (`_LANE_CLOSES_RE`). Returns the numbers it
    closed. An issue whose close fails is named on stderr and left out, so
    it stays open and gets no closing comment."""
    body = (view or {}).get("body", "") or ""
    closed = []
    for num in _LANE_CLOSES_RE.findall(body):
        res = _run_gh(["issue", "close", num])
        if res.returncode != 0:
            print(
                f"pr-merge: closing #{num} failed (gh exit {res.returncode}); "
                f"#{num} stays open, with no closing comment",
                file=sys.stderr,
            )
            continue
        closed.append(num)
    return closed


def _comment_on_closed_lane_issues(pr, closed, sha):
    """Criterion 27: on each issue `_close_lane_issues` closed, post a
    comment giving the lane PR number and the merge sha. A failed comment
    is named on stderr and never changes the exit code: the merge is
    already confirmed."""
    merge_sha = sha or "not reported by the GitHub API"
    for num in closed:
        res = _run_gh([
            "issue", "comment", num, "--body",
            f"Closed by lane PR #{pr} on merge (merge sha {merge_sha}).",
        ])
        if res.returncode != 0:
            print(
                f"pr-merge: closed #{num}, but its closing comment failed (gh exit {res.returncode})",
                file=sys.stderr,
            )


def _do_confirm(pr, deadline, start):
    trace = _load_trace()

    existing = _existing_pr_merged_span(trace, pr)
    if existing:
        # IDEMPOTENCE GUARD (unchanged contract): no gh calls at all on the
        # already-recorded path — the verdict was already verified when the
        # original merge was recorded, so it is NOT re-checked here.
        print(f"pr-merge: PR #{pr} already recorded (span {existing.get('span_id')})")
        return 0

    approve_comment, view = _assert_verdict_or_refuse(pr)
    if approve_comment is None:
        return 1

    if _is_lane_pr(view):
        if not _assert_lane_model_or_refuse(pr, approve_comment):
            return 1
        if not _assert_lane_window_or_refuse(pr, view):
            return 1

    merged, sha = _poll_confirm_merged(pr, deadline)
    if not merged:
        print(_pending_message(pr), file=sys.stderr)
        return 3

    # Race-safety: re-check right before appending (another invocation may
    # have recorded it between our first check and now).
    existing = _existing_pr_merged_span(trace, pr)
    if existing:
        print(f"pr-merge: PR #{pr} already recorded (span {existing.get('span_id')})")
        return 0

    if _is_lane_pr(view):
        _comment_on_closed_lane_issues(pr, _close_lane_issues(view), sha)

    dur_ms = int((time.monotonic() - start) * 1000)
    attrs = {"pr": pr, "sha": sha} if sha else {"pr": pr}
    trace.emit_span(trace_id=f"pr-{pr}", kind="pr_merged", attrs=attrs, dur_ms=dur_ms)
    trace.emit_span(trace_id=f"pr-{pr}", kind="verdict", attrs=_verdict_attrs(pr, approve_comment))
    print(f"pr-merge: PR #{pr} merged sha={sha}")
    _chain_record_green(deadline, sha)
    return 0


def _do_default(pr, deadline, start):
    # VERDICT ASSERTION (ADR-0076 D3 / criterion 3a): refuse BEFORE any merge
    # attempt -- not just before recording -- when the PR lacks a reviewer
    # comment matching VERDICT: APPROVE.
    approve_comment, view = _assert_verdict_or_refuse(pr)
    if approve_comment is None:
        return 1

    if _is_lane_pr(view):
        if not _assert_lane_model_or_refuse(pr, approve_comment):
            return 1
        if not _assert_lane_window_or_refuse(pr, view):
            return 1

    merged_command_ok = False
    last_returncode = 1
    attempt = 0
    for attempt in range(1, MAX_ATTEMPTS + 1):
        # The merge command itself is a single cheap call — always attempt it
        # at least once regardless of remaining budget. The deadline only
        # bounds the (potentially slow) BEHIND-class retry cycle below.
        res = _run_gh(["pr", "merge", pr, "--squash", "--auto"])
        # Echo gh's output as UTF-8 bytes: now that `_run_gh` decodes UTF-8,
        # a character a cp1252 stdout cannot encode (e.g. U+2713) would
        # otherwise raise after a server-side merge and skip the recording
        # below. The echo is informational, so a failed write never aborts.
        try:
            _write_stdout_utf8(res.stdout or "")
        except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:
            print(f"pr-merge: could not echo gh output ({exc})", file=sys.stderr)
        sys.stderr.write(res.stderr)
        last_returncode = res.returncode
        if res.returncode == 0:
            merged_command_ok = True
            break
        if attempt == MAX_ATTEMPTS or time.monotonic() >= deadline:
            break
        # Recoverable BEHIND-class failure: update branch, wait for green CI
        # (bounded by the SAME shared deadline as everything else), retry.
        _run_gh(["pr", "update-branch", pr])
        _poll_checks_until_green(pr, deadline)

    if not merged_command_ok:
        # A non-zero gh exit is NOT proof no merge happened — gh can exit
        # non-zero AFTER a successful server-side merge (e.g. "Auto merge is
        # not allowed for this repository"). REST-check before concluding
        # failure so a real merge is never silently lost (slice #1100).
        merged_despite_gh_exit, _sha_despite_gh_exit = _check_merged_once(pr)
        if not merged_despite_gh_exit:
            print(f"pr-merge: gh pr merge did not succeed for PR #{pr} within budget; no span written", file=sys.stderr)
            # Exit 3 is reserved exclusively for the MERGE-PENDING contract —
            # never let a raw gh exit code collide with that meaning.
            return last_returncode if last_returncode not in (0, 3) else 1
        print(f"pr-merge: gh exited non-zero for PR #{pr} but REST confirms merged=true — proceeding", file=sys.stderr)

    trace = _load_trace()
    existing = _existing_pr_merged_span(trace, pr)
    if existing:
        print(f"pr-merge: PR #{pr} already recorded (span {existing.get('span_id')})")
        return 0

    merged, sha = _poll_confirm_merged(pr, deadline)
    if not merged:
        print(_pending_message(pr), file=sys.stderr)
        return 3

    if _is_lane_pr(view):
        _comment_on_closed_lane_issues(pr, _close_lane_issues(view), sha)

    dur_ms = int((time.monotonic() - start) * 1000)
    attrs = {"pr": pr, "sha": sha} if sha else {"pr": pr}
    trace.emit_span(trace_id=f"pr-{pr}", kind="pr_merged", attrs=attrs, dur_ms=dur_ms)
    trace.emit_span(trace_id=f"pr-{pr}", kind="verdict", attrs=_verdict_attrs(pr, approve_comment))
    print(f"pr-merge: PR #{pr} merged sha={sha} attempts={attempt} behind_retried={attempt - 1}")
    _chain_record_green(deadline, sha)
    return 0


def main(argv=None):
    argv = list(argv if argv is not None else sys.argv[1:])
    if not argv:
        print("usage: pr-merge [--confirm] <pr-number>", file=sys.stderr)
        return 64

    confirm_mode = False
    if argv[0] == "--confirm":
        confirm_mode = True
        argv = argv[1:]
        if not argv:
            print("usage: pr-merge --confirm <pr-number>", file=sys.stderr)
            return 64

    pr = argv[0]
    start = time.monotonic()
    deadline = start + BUDGET_S

    if confirm_mode:
        return _do_confirm(pr, deadline, start)
    return _do_default(pr, deadline, start)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
